---
title: "Welding III (Inert Gas)"
code: "WEL-136"
category: "welding"
credits: "2"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Studies Tungsten and metallic inert gas procedures and practices including principles of operation, shielding gasses, filler rods, process variations and applications, manual and automatic welding, equipment and safety. Lecture 1 hour. Laboratory 3 hours. Total 4 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
